<title>USA: Thermo Cardiosystems sets acquisition.</title>
<headline>Thermo Cardiosystems sets acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermo Cardiosystems Inc said Monday it plans to acquire International Technidyne Corp from Thermo Electron Corp, in exchange for about 3,356,000 shares of Thermo Cardiosystems stock.</p>
<p>This transaction is intended to be accounted for in a manner similar to the pooling-of-interest method, Thermo Cardiosystems said without explanation. The company now has about 36.7 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Based in Edison, N.J., ITC is a maker of coagulation and hematology-related instrumentation, diagnostics, and pharmaceuticals that serve the medical market. It had revenues of $34 million in 1996 with net income of $4.7 million.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
